.TH env_len 3
.SH NAME
env_len \- calculate the number of entries in an environment array
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <env.h>

.B size_t env_len(const char* const* \fIe\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env_len
counts the number of elements in the null-terminated array of strings \fIe\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of elements in the array (excluding the terminating NULL pointer).